    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "{\"intent\": \"Determine the duration of these urges and behaviors to differentiate between chronic conditions like OCD or schizophrenia and an acute episode like brief psychotic disorder.\", \"question\": \"How long have you been experiencing urges like this to arrange things in a",
      "targeted_symptom": "psychotic_symptoms_duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, see, the thing with the bags, that specific thing... I mean, it's not just the bags, it's the paperwork too. The run reports, the incident logs, the way they have to be stacked, the way the edges have to line up exactly parallel to the desk. If they aren't, the information gets... it gets contaminated. And the cameras, too. The security cameras at the station and the dashcams in the rigs. I started noticing them differently, you know? Like they were recording the wrong frequencies or something, so I had to start covering certain ones up or standing at very specific angles so they wouldn't mess with my head while I was trying to get the paperwork right. All of that—the cameras, the paperwork, the bags in the bay, everything that made the lieutenant so upset—it's all been happening for about two months now. Give or take a few days, but right around two months. Before that, things were fine, mostly fine, but these last two months, it's just been so clear to me how everything is connected and how careful I have to be with the arrangements. If I don't do it, I don't know who will, and then what happens to the station? It's a lot of responsibility, and I don't think they understand how crucial it's been these past eight weeks.",
